The issue is with the quoting: `nspname = "public"` uses double quotes which PostgreSQL interprets as column identifiers, not string literals. It should use single quotes: `nspname = 'public'`. This is the same issue in my manual cleanup script - I used escaped double quotes instead of single quotes.

But the conftest.py uses the same quoting (double quotes in the DO block). Wait, let me check what the actual conftest.py uses:

```python
def _drop_composite_types(conn):
    conn.execute(text("""
        DO $$ DECLARE r RECORD;
        BEGIN
            FOR r IN (SELECT t.typname FROM pg_type t JOIN pg_namespace n ON t.typnamespace = n.oid WHERE n.nspname = 'public' AND t.typtype = 'c' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_class c WHERE c.relname = t.typname AND c.relnamespace = t.typnamespace AND c.relkind = 'r'))
            LOOP
                EXECUTE 'DROP TYPE IF EXISTS ' || quote_ident(r.typname) || ' CASCADE';
            END LOOP;
        END $$;
    """))
```

Yes! The conftest uses single quotes around `'public'` in the DO block, which is correct. My manual Python test used double quotes.

Now the issue is just that the DB was dropped. Let me recreate it and run again.

